> Since, we're already storing the InputEvents associated with each Action in the input_map. This PR simply uses this to also store each InputEvent's last value.

Yeah, that's exactly the issue I have with the implementation. I don't think we should modify the InputEvent API only for our needs in the action mapping system.

The mapping from event to action does not necessarily need all data contained in the InputEvents we store. For example, we don't need the "pressed" status of an InputEventKey event to map a key press to an action, we would only need a key ID and probably a few other fields. But everything events provide aren't really needed for mapping an event to an action.

To be more precise, I think that, eventually, we should modify this struct (in input_map.h) by removing `Ref<InputEvent>` and replacing it by a custom structure:
```
	struct Action {
		int id;
		float deadzone;
		List<Ref<InputEvent>> inputs;
	};
```

But anyway, to simplify things for now, I think we should keep `Ref<InputEvent>` there for now, but, instead of storing values directly inside the event. So we should have something like that:
```
        struct EventMapping {
                // The values you need to store
                bool pressed;
                //etc, ...
		Ref<InputEvent> event;
        }
	struct Action {
		int id;
		float deadzone;
		List<EventMapping> inputs;
	};
```
That way, we don't bloat the InputEvent API and keep the fix where it is needed.
